SAUNet lowers ConvNeXt-T error on ImageNet-C from 47.5 \% to 37.8 \%, ViT-S from 46.1 \% to 38.4 \% and NF-ResNet-50 from 63.2 \% to 51.0 \%. Across the $15 \times 5$ corruption grid SAUNet wins 82 \% of the cells against the best competing baseline. Throughput ratio $C(g) = 1.02 \pm 0.02$ and FLOP overhead 1.5 \% confirm negligible cost. Tiny-ImageNet-C shows similar 9-12 pp gains, while ImageNet-A accuracy rises from 51.9 \% (UniTTA-0G) to 56.7 \%.  
